  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# Lines in, a report out — and the program that shows what `as` is FOR.", "line": 1, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 2, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# Corpus and regression material (CLAUDE.md §9). The gap was measured on", "line": 3, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# Measured: `use ... as` appeared **once** in all of `examples/`, in", "line": 4, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# `examples/shapes/main.hero`, where it renames a module that did not have to", "line": 5, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# be renamed. That use is real and it is not the feature's warrant.", "line": 6, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 7, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# **THIS ONE CANNOT BE WRITTEN WITHOUT IT.** The program reads from", "line": 8, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# `read/source` and writes to `write/source`. Both paths end in `source`, so", "line": 9, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# both would bind `source` in this file, and `spec:11` refuses a file that", "line": 10, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# binds one name twice. There is no single rename that fixes it, because the", "line": 11, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# collision is between two modules and not between a module and a local: one", "line": 12, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# of them must be called something else HERE, which is exactly the case panel", "line": 13, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# 100 recorded as the alias's justification — *\"two published modules ending", "line": 14, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# in `client`, whose authors own neither the other's files nor a manifest to", "line": 15, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# put a rename in\"*. The two directories here stand in for those two", "line": 16, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# packages.", "line": 17, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 18, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# Panel 101 then refused binding the whole joined path (`read_source` and", "line": 19, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# `write_source`, which would need no alias) on the one argument no other seat", "line": 20, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# made: the last-part rule is reversible and the joined rule is not. This", "line": 21, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# program is what the refusal costs, written out — one `as` clause — and that", "line": 22, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# is the trade the record says was taken deliberately.", "line": 23, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 24, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# What it also pins, since a program that exists may as well earn twice: a", "line": 25, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# drive loop over a `T?` rather than over an index, `break` on a condition", "line": 26, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# inside it, and `chars()` doing the splitting in the reader.", "line": 27, "col": 1},
